; compiler-correctness bridge: evaluating an expression tree = summing its flattened leaves.
; eval e = sum(flatten e), where eval folds (+) over the tree and flatten lists the leaves left-to-right. By tree induction: Leaf v -> sum[v]=v+0=v=eval; Node l r -> flatten distributes over append, sum-append splits the sum, and the two IHs close it. The AST-semantics-equals-linear-fold theorem -- exactly the equivalence a verified compiler's lowering must preserve.
